1442:     ///
1443:     /// When `segment_uuids` is present, only those physical index segments are opened and their
1444:     /// current fragment coverage defines the count scope. That coverage is accepted only when the
1445:     /// selection includes every segment that contributes to it. After a fragment-reuse rewrite, one
1446:     /// source segment can advertise every destination fragment while still depending on sibling
1447:     /// segments; an incomplete selection is rejected. A supplied `fragment_ids` list must exactly
1448:     /// equal the selected segments' current coverage.
1449:     #[instrument(skip_all)]
